codex
I found a deadline-handling edge case in `seedAccounts`: the identity timer can fire just before the setup clock considers the budget expired. In a read-only, in-memory probe, 2 of 50 active signup timeouts returned bare `identity deadline exceeded`, without the required partial-accounts warning. I’m checking it at the regression test’s 30 ms deadline.

